  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0396, and it contains seven tables. The tables are User_Table, Guide_Table, Restaurant_Table, Hotel_Table, Scenic_Spot_Table, Route, and Write_Guide_Table.\nThe User_Table contains four columns: Nickname, Password, Profile_Picture, and Username. The Username column is the primary key and is a string with a maximum length of 255 characters. The other columns are strings with a maximum length of 255 characters.\nThe Guide_Table contains four columns: Category, Content, Guide_Title, and Tags. The Guide_Title column is the primary key and is a string with a maximum length of 255 characters. The other columns are strings with a maximum length of 255 characters.\nThe Restaurant_Table contains four columns: Image, Introduction, Location, and Restaurant_Name. The Restaurant_Name column is the primary key and is a string with a maximum length of 255 characters. The other columns are strings with a maximum length of 255 characters.\nThe Hotel_Table contains four columns: Hotel_Name, Image, Introduction, and Location. The Hotel_Name column is the primary key and is a string with a maximum length of 255 characters. The other columns are strings with a maximum length of 255 characters.\nThe Scenic_Spot_Table contains eight columns: Address, Days, Image, Introduction, Opening_Hours, Scenic_Spot_Name, Tips, and Tags. The Scenic_Spot_Name column is the primary key and is a string with a maximum length of 255 characters. The other columns are strings with a maximum length of 255 characters.\nThe Route table contains three columns: Content, Introduction, and Route_Name. The Route_Name column is the primary key and is a string with a maximum length of 255 characters. The other columns are strings with a maximum length of 255 characters.\nThe Write_Guide_Table contains three columns: Guide_Title, Username, and PRIMARY KEY. The PRIMARY KEY is a composite key consisting of Username and Guide_Title. The Guide_Title column is a string with a maximum length of 255 characters, and the Username column is a string with a maximum length of 255 characters.\nThe Write_Guide_Table has two foreign keys: Guide_Title and Username. The Guide_Title foreign key references the Guide_Title column in the Guide_Table, and the Username foreign key references the Username column in the User_Table. The foreign keys have update and delete rules of CASCADE.",
  "gold_question": "The main functions of a certain tourism information management system include:\n1. User management: including the management of user names, passwords, avatars, nicknames and other information. Users can write guides.\n2. Guide management: including the management of guide titles, categories, tags, content and other information.\n3. Hotel management: including the management of hotel names, introductions, pictures, locations and other information.\n4. Hotel management: including the management of hotel names, introductions, pictures, locations and other information.\n5. Attraction management: including the management of attraction names, introductions, pictures, addresses, opening hours, tips, days and other information.\n6. Route management: including the management of route names, content, tags, introductions and other information.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0396.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0396\nCREATE TABLE `user_table` (\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `nickname` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `profile_picture` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`username`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `guide_table` (\n  `guide_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `content` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `tags` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`guide_title`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `restaurant_table` (\n  `restaurant_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `image` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `introduction` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`restaurant_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `hotel_table` (\n  `hotel_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `image` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `introduction` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`hotel_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `scenic_spot_table` (\n  `scenic_spot_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `days` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `image` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `introduction` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `opening_hours` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `tips` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `tags` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`scenic_spot_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `route` (\n  `route_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `introduction` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`route_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `write_guide_table` (\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `guide_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`username`, `guide_title`),\n  CONSTRAINT `write_guide_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`guide_title`) REFERENCES `guide_table` (`guide_title`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `write_guide_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`username`) REFERENCES `user_table` (`username`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
